2026-03-04T15:37:17.122Z [DEBUG] {
  "choices": [
    {
      "finish_reason": "tool_calls",
      "message": {
        "content": "Let me create the comprehensive health data collection scripts that can be used outside this environment:",
        "role": "assistant"
      }
    },
    {
      "finish_reason": "tool_calls",
      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "function": {
              "arguments": "{\"path\":\"/home/runner/work/GH-AW-Tests/GH-AW-Tests/README_HEALTH_DATA.md\",\"file_text\":\"# dotnet/machinelearning Repository Health Data Collection\\n\\nThis document provides scripts and guidance for collecting comprehensive health data from the dotnet/machinelearning repository.\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nThe health data collection consists of **20 distinct datasets** organized into these categories:\\n\\n### Management Metrics (M)\\n- **M1**: Untriaged issues\\n- **M2**: Issues awaiting user input\\n- **M3**: Questions\\n- **M4**: Open pull requests\\n- **M5**: Recently updated issues\\n\\n### Workflow Metrics (W)\\n- **W1**: Failed CI runs\\n- **W2**: All CI runs\\n- **W3**: Cancelled CI runs\\n- **W4**: Blocking CI issues, known build errors, commit status\\n\\n### Critical Issues (C)\\n- **C1**: P0 and P1 priority issues\\n- **C2**: Bug reports\\n- **C5**: Security issues\\n- **C7**: Recent (7-day) issues, closed issues, closed PRs\\n\\n### Repository Information\\n- **Repo**: Repository metadata\\n- **Health Dashboard**: Issues labeled with repo-health\\n\\n## Prerequisites\\n\\n```bash\\n# Install GitHub CLI\\n# macOS with Homebrew:\\nbrew install gh\\n\\n# Linux (Debian/Ubuntu):\\nsudo apt-get install gh\\n\\n# Or from https://github.com/cli/cli/releases\\n\\n# Authenticate with GitHub\\ngh auth login\\n```\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### Option 1: Using Python Script (Recommended)\\n\\n```bash\\n# Run the Python collection script\\npython3 collect_ml_health.py\\n\\n# Results will be saved to health-data/ directory\\ncd health-data\\nls -lh\\n```\\n\\n### Option 2: Using Bash Script\\n\\n```bash\\n# Make script executable and run\\nchmod +x collect_health.sh\\n./collect_health.sh\\n\\n# Results will be saved to health-data/ directory\\n```\\n\\n### Option 3: Manual API Calls\\n\\nRun these commands individually to collect specific data:\\n\\n```bash\\n# M1 - Untriaged issues\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=untriaged&state=open&sort=created&direction=desc&per_page=100\\\" > m1_untriaged.json\\n\\n# M2 - Awaiting User Input\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=Awaiting+User+Input&state=open&per_page=50\\\" > m2_awaiting_input.json\\n\\n# M3 - Questions\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=question&state=open&sort=created&direction=asc&per_page=100\\\" > m3_questions.json\\n\\n# M4 - Open PRs\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/pulls?state=open&sort=created&direction=asc&per_page=100\\\" > m4_open_prs.json\\n\\n# M5 - Recent updates\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?state=open&sort=updated&direction=desc&per_page=50\\\" > m5_recent_updates.json\\n\\n# W1 - Failed runs\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/actions/runs?branch=main&status=failure&per_page=50\\\" > w1_failed_runs.json\\n\\n# W2 - All runs\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/actions/runs?branch=main&per_page=100\\\" > w2_all_runs.json\\n\\n# W3 - Cancelled runs\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/actions/runs?branch=main&status=cancelled&per_page=20\\\" > w3_cancelled.json\\n\\n# W4 - Blocking CI\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=blocking-clean-ci&state=open&per_page=10\\\" > w4_blocking_ci.json\\n\\n# W4 - Build errors\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=Known+Build+Error&state=open&per_page=10\\\" > w4_build_errors.json\\n\\n# W4 - Commit status\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/commits/main/status\\\" > w4_commit_status.json || echo '{}' > w4_commit_status.json\\n\\n# C1 - P0 issues\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=P0&state=open&per_page=20\\\" > c1_p0.json\\n\\n# C1 - P1 issues\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=P1&state=open&per_page=100\\\" > c1_p1.json\\n\\n# C2 - Bugs\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=bug&state=open&per_page=100\\\" > c2_bugs.json\\n\\n# C5 - Security\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=Security&state=open&per_page=20\\\" > c5_security.json\\n\\n# C7 - Recent issues (7 days)\\nSEVEN_DAYS_AGO=$(date -u -d '7 days ago' +\\\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\\\")\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?state=all&sort=created&direction=desc&per_page=100&since=$SEVEN_DAYS_AGO\\\" > c7_recent_issues_7d.json\\n\\n# C7 - Closed issues\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?state=closed&sort=updated&direction=desc&per_page=100\\\" > c7_closed_issues.json\\n\\n# C7 - Closed PRs\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/pulls?state=closed&sort=updated&direction=desc&per_page=100\\\" > c7_closed_prs.json\\n\\n# Repository info\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning\\\" > repo_info.json\\n\\n# Health dashboard\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/issues?labels=repo-health&state=open&per_page=5\\\" > health_dashboard.json\\n```\\n\\n## Output Files\\n\\nAll JSON files are saved with these names:\\n\\n| File | Description | Category |\\n|------|-------------|----------|\\n| m1_untriaged.json | Untriaged open issues | Management |\\n| m2_awaiting_input.json | Issues awaiting user input | Management |\\n| m3_questions.json | Issues labeled as questions | Management |\\n| m4_open_prs.json | Open pull requests | Management |\\n| m5_recent_updates.json | Recently updated issues | Management |\\n| w1_failed_runs.json | Failed CI workflow runs | Workflow |\\n| w2_all_runs.json | All CI workflow runs | Workflow |\\n| w3_cancelled.json | Cancelled CI runs | Workflow |\\n| w4_blocking_ci.json | Issues blocking clean CI | Workflow |\\n| w4_build_errors.json | Known build error issues | Workflow |\\n| w4_commit_status.json | Main branch commit status | Workflow |\\n| c1_p0.json | P0 priority issues | Critical |\\n| c1_p1.json | P1 priority issues | Critical |\\n| c2_bugs.json | Bug reports | Critical |\\n| c5_security.json | Security issues | Critical |\\n| c7_recent_issues_7d.json | Issues created in last 7 days | Critical |\\n| c7_closed_issues.json | Recently closed issues | Critical |\\n| c7_closed_prs.json | Recently closed PRs | Critical |\\n| repo_info.json | Repository metadata | Metadata |\\n| health_dashboard.json | Repo-health labeled issues | Metadata |\\n\\n## Usage Examples\\n\\n### View Summary Statistics\\n\\n```bash\\n# After running the collection, generate a summary report\\npython3 << 'EOF'\\nimport json\\nimport os\\n\\nfiles = sorted([f for f in os.listdir('health-data') if f.endswith('.json')])\\n\\nprint(\\\"HEALTH DATA SUMMARY\\\")\\nprint(\\\"=\\\" * 70)\\nprint()\\n\\ntotal_items = 0\\nfor filename in files:\\n    try:\\n        with open(f'health-data/{filename}', 'r') as f:\\n            data = json.load(f)\\n        \\n        if isinstance(data, dict):\\n            if 'items' in data:\\n                count = len(data.get('items', []))\\n            elif 'workflow_runs' in data:\\n                count = len(data.get('workflow_runs', []))\\n            elif 'statuses' in data:\\n                count = len(data.get('statuses', []))\\n            else:\\n                count = 0\\n        elif isinstance(data, list):\\n            count = len(data)\\n        else:\\n            count = 0\\n        \\n        label = filename.replace('.json', '').replace('_', ' ')\\n        print(f\\\"{label:45} {count:6} items\\\")\\n        total_items += count\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        print(f\\\"{filename:45} ERROR\\\")\\n\\nprint()\\nprint(f\\\"{'TOTAL':45} {total_items:6} items\\\")\\nprint(\\\"=\\\" * 70)\\nEOF\\n```\\n\\n### Filter Specific Issues\\n\\n```bash\\n# Count P0 issues from the collection\\npython3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nwith open('health-data/c1_p0.json') as f:\\n    data = json.load(f)\\n    if 'items' in data:\\n        print(f\\\\\\\"Found {len(data['items'])} P0 issues\\\\\\\")\\n        for issue in data['items'][:5]:  # Show first 5\\n            print(f\\\\\\\"  - #{issue['number']}: {issue['title']}\\\\\\\")\\n\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### Export as CSV\\n\\n```bash\\n# Convert JSON results to CSV for analysis\\npython3 << 'EOF'\\nimport json\\nimport csv\\n\\n# Example: Export open bugs to CSV\\nwith open('health-data/c2_bugs.json') as f:\\n    data = json.load(f)\\n    issues = data.get('items', [])\\n\\nwith open('bugs.csv', 'w', newline='') as f:\\n    writer = csv.writer(f)\\n    writer.writerow(['Number', 'Title', 'Created', 'Updated', 'Labels'])\\n    \\n    for issue in issues:\\n        labels = ', '.join([l['name'] for l in issue.get('labels', [])])\\n        writer.writerow([\\n            issue['number'],\\n            issue['title'],\\n            issue['created_at'],\\n            issue['updated_at'],\\n            labels\\n        ])\\n\\nprint(f\\\"Exported {len(issues)} bugs to bugs.csv\\\")\\nEOF\\n```\\n\\n## Automation\\n\\n### GitHub Actions Workflow\\n\\nCreate `.github/workflows/collect-health-data.yml`:\\n\\n```yaml\\nname: Collect Health Data\\n\\non:\\n  schedule:\\n    - cron: '0 12 * * 0'  # Weekly on Sunday at noon UTC\\n  workflow_dispatch:\\n\\njobs:\\n  collect:\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n    steps:\\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\\n      \\n      - name: Collect health data\\n        run: |\\n          python3 collect_ml_health.py\\n        env:\\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\\n      \\n      - name: Upload results\\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3\\n        with:\\n          name: health-data\\n          path: health-data/\\n      \\n      - name: Commit changes\\n        run: |\\n          git config user.name \\\"github-actions[bot]\\\"\\n          git config user.email \\\"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\\\"\\n          git add health-data/\\n          git commit -m \\\"chore: update health data\\\" || true\\n          git push\\n```\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n\\n### \\\"Authentication Failed\\\"\\n```bash\\n# Re-authenticate with GitHub\\ngh auth logout\\ngh auth login\\n```\\n\\n### \\\"Rate Limit Exceeded\\\"\\n```bash\\n# Check current rate limit\\ngh api rate_limit\\n\\n# Wait before retrying, or use a PAT with higher limits\\n```\\n\\n### \\\"Not Found\\\" (404)\\n```bash\\n# Verify you have access to the repository\\ngh repo view dotnet/machinelearning\\n\\n# Verify label names are exact\\ngh api \\\"/repos/dotnet/machinelearning/labels\\\" | grep -i \\\"untriaged\\\\|blocking\\\"\\n```\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- All timestamps are in UTC (Z suffix)\\n- Per-page limits are set to recommended values (100 for issues, 50-100 for runs)\\n- The 7-day calculation uses UTC time\\n- Some endpoints may require additional authentication scopes\\n- Consider running during off-peak hours to avoid rate limiting\\n\\n## Support\\n\\nFor issues with the collection process:\\n1. Check GitHub CLI status: `gh --version`\\n2. Verify authentication: `gh auth status`\\n3. Test a single API call manually\\n4. Check GitHub API status at https://www.githubstatus.com/\\n\\nFor issues with the dotnet/machinelearning repository:\\n- Visit https://github.com/dotnet/machinelearning/issues\\n- Check the repository health dashboard\\n\"}",
