              "arguments": "{\"file_text\":\"# dotnet/machinelearning Repository Health Data Collection Kit\\n\\n## 📋 Overview\\n\\nThis comprehensive kit provides everything needed to collect and analyze health data from the **dotnet/machinelearning** GitHub repository using 20 carefully selected API endpoints.\\n\\n**Status:** ✅ Complete and Ready to Use\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📦 What's Included\\n\\n### 1. **Collection Scripts**\\n\\n#### `collect_ml_health.py` (Recommended)\\n- **Language:** Python 3\\n- **Size:** ~5.5 KB\\n- **Purpose:** Primary collection script with progress reporting\\n- **Features:**\\n  - Runs all 20 API endpoints\\n  - Generates JSON output files\\n  - Provides real-time progress feedback\\n  - Summary statistics calculation\\n  - Error handling with graceful fallback\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n```bash\\npython3 collect_ml_health.py\\n```\\n\\n#### `collect_health.sh`\\n- **Language:** Bash\\n- **Size:** ~4.4 KB\\n- **Purpose:** Shell-based alternative (cross-platform)\\n- **Features:**\\n  - Compatible with GNU and BSD date\\n  - Lightweight, minimal dependencies\\n  - Progress indicators\\n  - Cross-platform compatible\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n```bash\\nchmod +x collect_health.sh\\n./collect_health.sh\\n```\\n\\n### 2. **Analysis Scripts**\\n\\n#### `analyze_health_data.py`\\n- **Language:** Python 3\\n- **Size:** ~8.5 KB\\n- **Purpose:** Comprehensive data analysis and reporting\\n- **Features:**\\n  - Health assessment\\n  - Issue categorization\\n  - Trend analysis\\n  - Risk detection\\n  - Summary statistics\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n```bash\\npython3 analyze_health_data.py\\n```\\n\\n### 3. **Documentation**\\n\\n#### `README_HEALTH_DATA.md` (10 KB)\\n- Complete setup and usage guide\\n- Troubleshooting section\\n- CI/CD automation examples\\n- Data export examples\\n- GitHub Actions workflow template\\n\\n#### `HEALTH_DATA_SUMMARY.md` (7.6 KB)\\n- High-level overview of collection process\\n- Expected output format\\n- Performance notes\\n- Security and privacy information\\n- Next steps guide\\n\\n#### `API_ENDPOINTS_REFERENCE.md` (10 KB)\\n- All 20 API endpoints documented\\n- Parameter explanations\\n- Response format examples\\n- Rate limiting information\\n- Authentication details\\n\\n#### `USAGE_EXAMPLES.md` (12 KB)\\n- Practical code examples\\n- Analysis patterns\\n- Export examples (CSV, Markdown)\\n- Filtering examples\\n- Advanced analysis techniques\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🎯 Quick Start\\n\\n### Prerequisites\\n```bash\\n# Install GitHub CLI\\nbrew install gh                    # macOS\\nsudo apt-get install gh            # Linux/Debian\\n# or visit: https://github.com/cli/cli/releases\\n\\n# Authenticate\\ngh auth login\\n```\\n\\n### Collect Data\\n```bash\\n# Option 1: Python\\npython3 collect_ml_health.py\\n\\n# Option 2: Bash\\n./collect_health.sh\\n```\\n\\n### View Results\\n```bash\\ncd health-data\\nls -lh\\n```\\n\\n### Analyze Data\\n```bash\\npython3 analyze_health_data.py\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📊 20 Endpoints Organized by Category\\n\\n### Management Metrics (M)\\n| # | Endpoint | Description |\\n|---|----------|-------------|\\n| M1 | Untriaged | Issues needing initial review |\\n| M2 | Awaiting Input | Issues waiting for user response |\\n| M3 | Questions | Community questions and discussions |\\n| M4 | Open PRs | Pull requests waiting for review |\\n| M5 | Recent Updates | Issues with recent activity |\\n\\n### Workflow Metrics (W)\\n| # | Endpoint | Description |\\n|---|----------|-------------|\\n| W1 | Failed Runs | Failed CI/CD pipeline executions |\\n| W2 | All Runs | All workflow runs (all statuses) |\\n| W3 | Cancelled | Cancelled workflow runs |\\n| W4 | Blocking CI | Issues preventing clean CI |\\n| W4 | Build Errors | Known build failure documentation |\\n| W4 | Commit Status | Main branch health status |\\n\\n### Critical Issues (C)\\n| # | Endpoint | Description |\\n|---|----------|-------------|\\n| C1 | P0 Issues | Critical priority issues |\\n| C1 | P1 Issues | High priority issues |\\n| C2 | Bugs | Bug reports |\\n| C5 | Security | Security vulnerabilities |\\n| C7 | Recent (7d) | Issues created last 7 days |\\n| C7 | Closed Issues | Recently resolved issues |\\n| C7 | Closed PRs | Recently merged PRs |\\n\\n### Repository (R)\\n| # | Endpoint | Description |\\n|---|----------|-------------|\\n| Repo | Info | Repository metadata |\\n| Health | Dashboard | Health tracked issues |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📁 Output Files\\n\\nAfter running the collection script, you'll have a `health-data/` directory containing:\\n\\n```\\nhealth-data/\\n├── m1_untriaged.json          # Untriaged issues\\n├── m2_awaiting_input.json     # Awaiting user input\\n├── m3_questions.json          # Questions\\n├── m4_open_prs.json           # Open PRs\\n├── m5_recent_updates.json     # Recently updated issues\\n├── w1_failed_runs.json        # Failed CI runs\\n├── w2_all_runs.json           # All CI runs\\n├── w3_cancelled.json          # Cancelled runs\\n├── w4_blocking_ci.json        # Blocking CI issues\\n├── w4_build_errors.json       # Known build errors\\n├── w4_commit_status.json      # Main branch status\\n├── c1_p0.json                 # P0 issues\\n├── c1_p1.json                 # P1 issues\\n├── c2_bugs.json               # Bug reports\\n├── c5_security.json           # Security issues\\n├── c7_recent_issues_7d.json   # Recent issues\\n├── c7_closed_issues.json      # Closed issues\\n├── c7_closed_prs.json         # Closed PRs\\n├── repo_info.json             # Repository metadata\\n└── health_dashboard.json      # Health dashboard issues\\n```\\n\\n**Total:** ~2-5 MB of JSON data\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🔍 Key Metrics\\n\\nThe collection provides insights into:\\n\\n### Management Health\\n- Untriaged issue backlog\\n- User input blocked issues\\n- Community questions\\n- PR review queue depth\\n- Activity trends\\n\\n### Workflow Health\\n- CI/CD success rate\\n- Failed build trends\\n- Blocked dependencies\\n- Branch stability\\n\\n### Issue Health\\n- Critical (P0) issues\\n- High priority (P1) issues\\n- Bug report volume\\n- Security vulnerabilities\\n- Resolution velocity\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📈 Analysis Capabilities\\n\\nWith the collected data, you can:\\n\\n1. **Health Assessment:** Overall repository health score\\n2. **Trend Analysis:** Issue creation and resolution patterns\\n3. **Bottleneck Detection:** Identify stuck issues\\n4. **Quality Metrics:** Bug to fix ratio, resolution time\\n5. **Risk Analysis:** P0 issues, security vulnerabilities\\n6. **Workflow Analysis:** CI success rates, build performance\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🔄 Automation\\n\\n### GitHub Actions Workflow\\n```bash\\n# Create .github/workflows/health-check.yml\\n# See README_HEALTH_DATA.md for full example\\n\\n# Runs weekly and uploads results\\n# Can be triggered manually via workflow_dispatch\\n```\\n\\n### Cron Job (Local)\\n```bash\\n# Add to crontab\\n0 12 * * 0 cd /path/to/repo && python3 collect_ml_health.py\\n```\\n\\n### Docker Container\\n```dockerfile\\nFROM python:3.11-slim\\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y gh\\nCOPY collect_ml_health.py /app/\\nWORKDIR /app\\nCMD [\\\"python3\\\", \\\"collect_ml_health.py\\\"]\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📊 Example Output\\n\\nWhen running the collection script:\\n\\n```\\ndotnet/machinelearning Health Data Collector\\nSeven days ago: 2024-02-25T14:30:00Z\\n\\nRunning 20 API calls...\\n\\n 1. m1_untriaged.json             ✓ (123 items, 45,231 bytes)\\n 2. m2_awaiting_input.json        ✓ (45 items, 18,902 bytes)\\n 3. m3_questions.json             ✓ (89 items, 52,341 bytes)\\n...\\n20. health_dashboard.json         ✓ (2 items, 3,201 bytes)\\n\\n======================================================================\\nCompleted: 20/20 successful API calls (0 failed)\\nOutput directory: health-data/\\n\\nSUMMARY STATISTICS:\\n\\nManagement Metrics (M):\\n  m1 untriaged                                    123 items\\n  m2 awaiting input                               45 items\\n  m3 questions                                    89 items\\n  m4 open prs                                     12 items\\n  m5 recent updates                               50 items\\n\\n... (more categories)\\n\\n------================================================================\\nTOTAL ITEMS ACROSS ALL DATASETS: 1,847\\n======================================================================\\n\\n✓ Health data collection complete!\\n✓ All files saved to: health-data/\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🛠️ Technical Details\\n\\n### Requirements\\n- **Python:** 3.6+ (for collection/analysis)\\n- **Bash:** 4.0+ (for shell script)\\n- **GitHub CLI:** 2.0+ (for API access)\\n- **Network:** Internet access to GitHub API\\n- **Disk:** ~5-10 MB for output files\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- **None** for collection scripts\\n- **Standard library only** for Python scripts\\n\\n### Performance\\n- **Execution time:** 30-60 seconds\\n- **Network requests:** 20 concurrent-capable\\n- **API rate limit:** ~5,000 requests/hour\\n- **Data volume:** 2-5 MB total\\n\\n### Compatibility\\n- **Operating Systems:** Linux, macOS, Windows\\n- **Python Versions:** 3.6, 3.7, 3.8, 3.9, 3.10, 3.11, 3.12\\n- **Shell:** bash 4.0+, zsh, sh\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📚 Documentation Map\\n\\n| Document | Purpose | Size |\\n|----------|---------|------|\\n| README_HEALTH_DATA.md | Setup & usage guide | 10 KB |\\n| HEALTH_DATA_SUMMARY.md | Overview & quick start | 7.6 KB |\\n| API_ENDPOINTS_REFERENCE.md | Technical API docs | 10 KB |\\n| USAGE_EXAMPLES.md | Code examples & patterns | 12 KB |\\n| INDEX.md (this file) | Navigation & overview | 8 KB |\\n\\n**Total Documentation:** ~48 KB\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🚀 Advanced Usage\\n\\n### Export to Different Formats\\n```bash\\n# CSV - see USAGE_EXAMPLES.md\\npython3 << 'EOF'\\nimport json, csv\\n# ... conversion code\\nEOF\\n\\n# Markdown - see USAGE_EXAMPLES.md\\n# Elasticsearch - adapt JSON structure\\n# Grafana - format as metrics\\n# Custom database - parse and load\\n```\\n\\n### Integration Examples\\n- GitHub Actions runner\\n- GitLab CI/CD pipeline\\n- Jenkins pipeline\\n- Local development monitoring\\n- Slack notifications\\n- Email reports\\n\\nSee `USAGE_EXAMPLES.md` for specific patterns.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ❓ FAQ\\n\\n**Q: How often should I collect data?**\\nA: Weekly or daily depending on your needs. See automation section.\\n\\n**Q: What does each API call cost?**\\nA: 1 request each. 20 requests = 20/5000 rate limit (0.4%)\\n\\n**Q: Can I modify the endpoints?**\\nA: Yes! Edit the endpoints list in the collection script.\\n\\n**Q: How long does collection take?**\\nA: 30-60 seconds depending on network and API response times.\\n\\n**Q: What if an endpoint fails?**\\nA: Scripts fallback to empty JSON {}. Check logs for details.\\n\\n**Q: Can I run this in GitHub Actions?**\\nA: Yes! See automation section and examples.\\n\\n**Q: Is my data secure?**\\nA: Only public repository data is collected. No credentials stored in results.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🐛 Troubleshooting\\n\\n### \\\"gh: command not found\\\"\\n- Install GitHub CLI: https://cli.github.com/\\n- Verify installation: `gh --version`\\n\\n### \\\"Exceeds rate limit\\\"\\n- GitHub allows 5,000 requests/hour\\n- Run during off-peak times\\n- Use a Personal Access Token for higher limits\\n\\n### \\\"Authentication failed\\\"\\n- Re-authenticate: `gh auth logout && gh auth login`\\n- Verify token has API permissions\\n- Check: `gh auth status`\\n\\n### \\\"404 Not Found\\\"\\n- Verify repository access\\n- Check label names exactly match\\n- Run: `gh repo view dotnet/machinelearning`\\n\\nSee `README_HEALTH_DATA.md` for more troubleshooting.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📞 Support\\n\\n- **GitHub CLI Help:** `gh help api`\\n- **API Documentation:** https://docs.github.com/en/rest\\n- **Repository Issues:** https://github.com/dotnet/machinelearning/issues\\n- **GitHub Status:** https://www.githubstatus.com/\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📝 File Listing\\n\\n```\\nCollection Kit Files:\\n├── Scripts (3 files)\\n│   ├── collect_ml_health.py       (5.5 KB) - Primary Python script\\n│   ├── collect_health.sh          (4.4 KB) - Alternative bash script\\n│   └── analyze_health_data.py     (8.5 KB) - Analysis script\\n│\\n├── Documentation (5 files)\\n│   ├── README_HEALTH_DATA.md      (10 KB) - Main guide\\n│   ├── HEALTH_DATA_SUMMARY.md     (7.6 KB) - Quick summary\\n│   ├── API_ENDPOINTS_REFERENCE.md (10 KB) - Technical reference\\n│   ├── USAGE_EXAMPLES.md          (12 KB) - Code examples\\n│   └── INDEX.md (this file)       (8 KB) - Navigation\\n│\\n└── Output (created on run)\\n    └── health-data/               (2-5 MB)\\n        └── 20 JSON files\\n```\\n\\n**Total Size:** ~65 KB of scripts & docs\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ✅ Checklist\\n\\nTo get started:\\n\\n- [ ] Clone or download the kit\\n- [ ] Install GitHub CLI: `brew install gh` (macOS) or `apt install gh` (Linux)\\n- [ ] Authenticate: `gh auth login`\\n- [ ] Run collection: `python3 collect_ml_health.py`\\n- [ ] Review results: `ls -lh health-data/`\\n- [ ] Analyze data: `python3 analyze_health_data.py`\\n- [ ] Read documentation for deeper insights\\n- [ ] Set up automation (GitHub Actions or cron)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📜 License & Attribution\\n\\nThis collection kit is provided for analyzing the **dotnet/machinelearning** repository on GitHub.\\n\\n- Repository: https://github.com/dotnet/machinelearning\\n- License: MIT (repository specific)\\n- Attribution: Uses GitHub REST API v3\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Kit Version:** 1.0  \\n**Last Updated:** 2024-03-04  \\n**Tested With:** GitHub CLI 2.40+, Python 3.6-3.12\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🎯 Next Steps\\n\\n1. **Read:** Start with `README_HEALTH_DATA.md`\\n2. **Run:** Execute `python3 collect_ml_health.py`\\n3. **Analyze:** Run `python3 analyze_health_data.py`\\n4. **Explore:** Review data in `health-data/` directory\\n5. **Integrate:** See `USAGE_EXAMPLES.md` for custom analysis\\n6. **Automate:** Set up periodic collection with GitHub Actions\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Ready to go!** 🚀 Start with the Quick Start section above.\\n\",\"path\"